00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.370 align:start position:0%
 
hey guys it's Tony and Mike from  GameSpot Mike you just played two hours  of Red Dead Redemption - on PC coming  out on November 5th tell me  service-level what you thought yeah so  it is as you might have seen from the  launch trailer that came out a few days  ago or the environments trailer that  came out a couple weeks ago it looks  very good  it's obviously you know Rockstar puts a  lot of time and effort into their PC  releases because obviously Red Dead 2  came out last year in October but now  yeah like you said November 5th it's  released on PC it is it it feels like  Rockstar just showing off it's fairly  like breathtaking for the most part I'm  not traditionally like a someone who  gets super into visuals or graphics but  this is like hard not to notice  everything I pretty much when I first  started off I they gave me free rein to  do whatever I want but I did the noblest  of men and a woman quest which is where  if you recall you're going around to the  different gunslingers the famous  gunslingers to help this guy write a  biography about them and so I did that  question because they suggested Rockstar  suggests that do that because I would  see it takes you all over the map so I  went up to Flacco Hernandez in the snow  the snow was probably like the most  impressive area because the way that the  lighting blinds you on the snow growing  up in upstate New York I'm very aware of  how that can happen like if you're not  like paying attention and the snow is  reflect or the Sun is reflecting off the  snow and the right way you can fall off  a cliff because it's actually like  blinding you when I ran into these like  the evergreen trees with snow on the  boughs it would just like shed all the  snow and you could see like different  snowflakes kind of scurry off into the  air it's it was nuts and then also just  the the way that like clouds rolling  actually looks like a storm is coming  again red the two head clouds on you  know ps4 pro Xbox 1 X but these clouds  look like it's actually like you kind of  believe that a storm's rolling in you're  like I do not want to be up here when  these clouds rolling in Laboy in the  swampy area was just absolutely  astonishing in the way that light would  come through the trees or light would  reflect off the water you could kind of  see little individual eddies in the  rivers like I remember weeds actually  all looking different from one another  there is a lot of attention paid to this  and it already just I really want to  replay the entirety of the game despite  being I mean I like the game I know it's  pretty divisive but I love the game that  was my game of the year last year and I  do fully think I'm going to be playing  it again just to see all of this so a  wide array of graphical improvements  things like that but for those who maybe  aren't necessarily just looking for  better resolution there's also some new  content added to this version correct  yeah they'll have I mean there's like  kind of surface stuff like there are a  few new weapons I tried out one of the  new pistols which is good as you'd  imagine there's a new horse breed which  I got to try out and it was just like  you know like a lot of endurance very  fast so you'll have new stuff but also I  think the biggest thing for me is an  actual photo mode again speaking of the  gunslinger quest I mentioned you get the  camera in that quest then you could take  like diegetic photos with Arthur's  camera now there's an actual photo mode  you just I just press Start I press the  whatever the Xbox button is used to be  back now into the two squares the menu  button or whatever you go into photo  mode you can do free roam as long as you  don't go too far from Arthur there were  like pretty dizzying number of options  in terms of how it can mess with the  photos there's actual like effects where  you can do like a daguerreotype or a  negative so it could really get that  Wild West look like something that might  have been printed in like on wanted  posters and I took a few photos that  were just you know like depth of field  obviously like certain you know default  options that you almost always have but  the photo mode itself I can see this  becoming like that Ilona to draw for me  and again I'm not usually one to get  super excited about photo modes I mean  like I remember I've messed around with  it and like horizon zero down a little  bit and I always enjoy them they're a  great option but this game like it  deserves to have a photo mode I'd say  like the you can have like these like  environmental landscapes you can make  these like frescoes of Arthur and the in  the the world and it's it's just insane  like how many it was hard for me to get  a bad photo I mean like composition wise  is always you know like it's it's fun to  try to actually make it  photo but with like clouds rolling in  and then like especially with the  moonlight and Arthur being silhouetted  it's it's it's insane and it was I it's  hard not to talk about it without  sounding hyperbolic but it really is one  of the better-looking things I can  remember in a recent memory if not you  know like in general so yeah we will  have more on Red Dead Redemption 2 on PC  when it launched on November 5th we will  be covering that and if you're watching  this then we will have already you know  played a little bit of it like I said I  played a couple hours but I myself am  looking very much forward to playing  more of this and we'll have them on our  YouTube channel videos about it and I'm  sure other people in the office will be  playing it despite the bevy of games  we're covering this fall see you next  time guys  [Music]

